{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792570000000-engineer-p7m-lint-scan.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 08:00 +07\n# Task (codex): fix two red tests on the merged phase-7 branch; reviewed by a NON-codex reviewer (Fable) with mutants\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7m`, branch `srvm-phase7m` = integration branch `srvm-phase7` merged with current origin/master (which brought the other orchestrator's admission work: `yin.repl.link` is now `yin.vm.linker.interpreter`, `yin.repl.admission` is `yin.vm.linker.admission`; see `collab/1792286000000-orchestrator-note-linker-relocation.md`). Do not touch their files except to fix a require that conflicts with our work. Two reds in OUR seat:\n(1) JVM `dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test/architectural-lint-sweeps-production-sources` (`test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc:479`): the sweep forbids an equality comparison against dao.jing's DEFAULT minting vars (address validation must be algorithm-aware: use `segment-matches?` or the registry's verify path, never `(= address (jing/segment-key x))`, because an address may legitimately be SHA-256-minted). It flags at least `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` `decode*` and `check-install!` (and a third form, run the test to list all). Read the test's `flags-equality-validation?` to learn exactly what it flags, then fix each site in `rows.cljc` (and any other flagged production file) so validation is algorithm-aware where an address from outside is checked. IMPORTANT correctness question to settle in your report: for the CARRIER the row ids are BLAKE3 by construction (profile `{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}`); if a row id or a manifest address could arrive minted under another registered algorithm, say whether the code must accept it (verify under its own algorithm) or refuse it explicitly with a named kind (prefer: verify with `segment-matches?`/the algorithm the address names for dao.jing STORE addresses such as a manifest's `:yin.semantic/code` entry or a derivation record address; for the carrier's own row ids keep BLAKE3 and refuse a non-BLAKE3 id explicitly), and test it both ways (a SHA-256-addressed install image/record verifies; a carrier row id claiming sha256 is refused). No behaviour change otherwise: every existing root id and pin stays.\n(2) JVM and Node `yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test/scanners-agree-on-the-c4-modules` (`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scan_test.cljc:205`): the scanner output for the `[:c4 :py]` group no longer equals `scanner_goldens.cljc`. Determine WHY: print the diff between the scanner output and the golden for that group; check it is explained by the other orchestrator's C4/admission changes to the modules (git log -p over the C4 module sources since the goldens were last generated: `git log --oneline -- test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scanner_goldens.cljc`) and NOT by a scanner bug or by our rows/derive changes. If it is a legitimate consequence of module changes, regenerate that group's golden with the documented method (read the header of `scanner_goldens.cljc` and `scan_test.cljc` for how; keep the owner's rule: goldens are regenerated by a mechanical, recomputable procedure, never hand-edited) and put the diff and its explanation in the report; if it is a scanner bug, fix the scanner and say so. Do not regenerate other groups.\nAlso run `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (JVM) and report: master carries 08a3a722 which fixed that suite's readers for the admission default; shiva's Dart slow lane failed two of its tests on `srvm-phase7` BEFORE this merge: tell me if they pass here on the JVM.\nVerification, ALL foreground, JVM only: `clj -M:kondo --lint` on changed files; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test`; then every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace and the whole `dao.jing.*` family (report counts; the only acceptable remaining red is `cbor-conformance-test/no-source-file-that-names-the-resource-writes-files` IF it still fails on master, check). Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): revert each fixed site to the equality form (the lint must fail); a carrier row id with a non-BLAKE3 prefix accepted; a SHA-256 install address refused. Do not commit. Report `collab/1792570000000-engineer-p7m-lint-scan.report.md`: per site the change and why, the scan diff and explanation, counts, mutants, anything uncertain.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
