 digest for `(content-hash v {:algorithm :sha256})`.\"\n88:(def default-hash-algorithm\n89:  \"The default algorithm used for implicit minting (content-hash, segment-key,\n95:  \"The closed, immutable algorithm registry. Both initial entries produce\n105:(def ^:private algorithm-id-pattern\n139:  \"Digest host bytes bs with the specified algorithm keyword (:blake3, :sha256).\n140:   Returns lowercase hexadecimal string. Unknown algorithms throw.\"\n141:  [algorithm bs]\n142:  (case algorithm\n145:    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n146:                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n150:  \"Digest string s as UTF-8 bytes with the specified algorithm keyword.\n151:   Returns lowercase hexadecimal string. Unknown algorithms throw.\"\n152:  [algorithm s]\n153:  (case algorithm\n156:    (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algorithm)\n157:                    {:algorithm algorithm}))))\n164:   `(content-hash v {:algorithm algo})`.\n172:  \"Hash the canonical-bytes of v using the specified algorithm (defaulting to\n173:   default-hash-algorithm, i.e. :blake3). Returns lowercase hexadecimal string.\n174:   Arities: [v] and [v {:keys [algorithm]}].\"\n176:   (content-hash v {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n178:   (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)]\n184:   the payload: :segment/<algorithm-id>-<digest>.\n185:   The 1-arg form defaults to default-hash-algorithm (:blake3).\n186:   The 2-arg form accepts {:algorithm :sha256} (or any registered algorithm).\"\n188:   (segment-key v {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n190:   (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)\n193:       (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\n194:                       {:algorithm algo})))\n196:           digest (content-hash v {:algorithm algo})]\n200:(defn parse-segment-address\n202:   splits the name on the first `-` into algorithm identifier and digest,\n206:   Returns {:algorithm :<algo>, :digest \\\"<hex>\\\", :canonical :segment/...}\n216:            (when (re-matches algorithm-id-pattern algo-id)\n225:                        {:algorithm algo,\n232:   :segment/<algorithm>-<digest-hex>.\"\n234:  (boolean (parse-segment-address x)))\n237:(defn segment-algorithm\n238:  \"The algorithm keyword (:blake3, :sha256) carried by a segment address.\n241:  (if-let [parsed (parse-segment-address address)]\n242:    (:algorithm parsed)\n250:  (if-let [parsed (parse-segment-address address)]\n262:(defn segment-matches?\n265:   address-carried algorithm.\n266:   Never throws: malformed addresses, unknown algorithms, digest mismatches,\n269:  (if-let [{:keys [algorithm digest]} (parse-segment-address address)]\n272:            actual (digest-bytes algorithm bs)]\n282:   algorithm. Never throws: a malformed address, a foreign algorithm, or a\n285:  (if-let [{:keys [algorithm digest]} (parse-segment-address address)]\n287:      (= digest (digest-bytes algorithm bs))\n308:   under the address-carried algorithm; the byte-level twin of\n309:   segment-matches? for a backend that stores bytes and needs them.\n313:  (let [{:keys [algorithm digest]}\n314:        (or (parse-segment-address address)\n318:    (when-not (= digest (digest-bytes algorithm bs))\n326:   the address under its carried algorithm, then decodes exactly one\n331:  (let [{:keys [algorithm digest]}\n332:        (or (parse-segment-address address)\n335:    (when-not (= digest (digest-bytes algorithm bs))\n346:   the bytes must hash to the address under its carried algorithm, and\n375:   Supports [handle payload] (defaulting to default-hash-algorithm, :blake3)\n376:   and [handle payload {:keys [algorithm]}].\n396:   (materialize! handle payload {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n406:     (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)\n409:         (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\n410:                         {:algorithm algo})))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
