{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '330,357p' test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc; sed -n '315,380p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scan_test.cljc; sed -n '1,140p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc; sed -n '260,312p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc; head -35 test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc; git log --oneline 58dc0964..HEAD -- src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/1792286000000-orchestrator-note-linker-relocation.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '330,357p' test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc; sed -n '315,380p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/scan_test.cljc; sed -n '1,140p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc; sed -n '260,312p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc; head -35 test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc; git log --oneline 58dc0964..HEAD -- src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/1792286000000-orchestrator-note-linker-relocation.md\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- equality-form?\n  [form]\n  (and (seq? form)\n       (contains? #{'= 'not= 'clojure.core/= 'clojure.core/not=}\n                  (first form))))\n\n\n(defn- flags-equality-validation?\n  \"The lint's decision procedure: true when form is an equality/inequality\n   call with a target-var call directly among its operands. This is a\n   syntactic check over one form, matching the H0 charter (\\\"a static\n   check function / test that inspects ASTs or namespaces\\\") without\n   requiring a full analyzer pass; it walks nested forms so a target call\n   buried in a let-bound comparison is still found.\"\n  [form]\n  (letfn [(walk\n            [f]\n            (cond\n              (and (equality-form? f)\n                   (some validation-target-call? (rest f)))\n              true\n              (seq? f) (some walk f)\n              (coll? f) (some walk f)\n              :else false))]\n    (boolean (walk form))))\n\n\n(deftest architectural-lint-flags-equality-based-validation\n(deftest ^:slow goldens-match\n  (slow/guard \"goldens-match\"\n              (fn []\n                (doseq [[group programs] (all-programs)\n                        [n ast] programs]\n                  (testing [group n]\n                    (is (= (get-in goldens/scanner-goldens [group n]) (old-answer ast) (new-answer ast))))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow verify-outcomes-agree\n  (slow/guard \"verify-outcomes-agree\"\n              (fn []\n                (doseq [[group programs] (all-programs)\n                        [n ast] programs]\n                  (testing [group n]\n                    (is (= (:join (old-answer ast)) (:join (new-answer ast))))))\n                (is (= {:status :refused :reason :use-before-definition :name 'n}\n                       (:join (new-answer (second (last b0-programs)))))))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj (defn print-goldens\n          \"Generate the historical scanner fixture, without publishing modules.\"\n          []\n          (prn (into {} (map (fn [[group programs]]\n                               [group (into {} (map (fn [[n ast]] [n (old-answer ast)])) programs)]))\n                     [[:b0 b0-programs] [:register corpus/programs]\n                      [:c4 (mapv (fn [[n spec]] [n (:ast spec)]) (c4-specs))]]))))\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]))\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn task-node\n  [cursor-cells result]\n  (rows/node :task [3 rows/profile :halted :root 0 (rows/node :bindings [])\n                    (rows/node :store []) [] (rows/node :parked-table [])\n                    (rows/node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity cursor-cells)) {} {} [] [] nil result nil]))\n\n\n(defn cursor-cell-body\n  [stream position]\n  (rows/node :cursor-cell-body [(rows/node :stream [stream {:peer stream}]) position]))\n\n\n(defn fixture\n  [a b x y]\n  (let [payload [:row (rows/node :map\n                                 [[:lit 'both] [:row (rows/node :set [[:cursor-cell x] [:cursor-cell y]])]\n                                  [:lit 'one] [:cursor-cell x]\n                                  [:lit 'streams] [:row (rows/node :set [[:row (rows/node :stream [a {:peer a}])]\n                                                                         [:row (rows/node :stream [b {:peer b}])]])]\n                                  [:lit 'cursors] [:row (rows/node :map [[:cursor-cell x] [:lit :x] [:cursor-cell y] [:lit :y]])]])]\n        task (task-node [[x (cursor-cell-body a 0)] [y (cursor-cell-body b 0)]] [:lit nil])]\n    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots task) 6 (rows/node :store ['payload payload])))))\n\n\n(declare portable-frame)\n\n\n(defn- encoded\n  [x]\n  (cond (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/row)) [:row (:yin.k/row x)]\n        (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell)) [:cursor-cell (:yin.k/cursor-cell x)]\n        :else [:lit x]))\n\n\n(defn- portable-value\n  [m x]\n  ;; Classify native test values into the decoded codec domain. No seals\n  ;; travel. Captures retain their entire act and K; closures retain the\n  ;; code address, binders, lexical bindings and module context.\n  (cond\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    {:yin.k/row (rows/node :reified\n                           [(rows/decode (rows/frame->rows\n                                           (portable-frame m (ft/canonical m (values/payload x) false)) encoded))])}\n    (values/closure? x)\n    (let [p (values/payload x) e (:env p)]\n      {:yin.k/row (rows/node :closure [(get-in m [:code (:segment p) :address]) (:entry p) (:params p)\n                                       (rows/node :bindings\n                                                  (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (encoded (portable-value m v))])\n                                                          (sort #(cbor/encoded-compare (first %1) (first %2))\n                                                                (engine/without-store-of e))))\n                                       (engine/env-store-of e)])})\n    (fn? x) {:yin.k/row (rows/node :prim ['fixture/primitive])}\n    (and (map? x) (= :cursor-ref (:type x))) {:yin.k/cursor-cell (:id x)}\n    (and (map? x) (= :stream-ref (:type x))) {:yin.k/row (rows/node :stream [(:id x) :fixture/served])}\n    (coll? x)\n    (let [kind (cond (map? x) :map (vector? x) :vec (set? x) :set :else :list)\n          xs (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x)\n          vs (mapv #(encoded (portable-value m %)) xs)]\n      (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) vs)\n        {:yin.k/row (rows/node kind vs)}\n        x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn portable-frame\n  [m f]\n  (let [bindings (fn [mappings] (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (portable-value m v)])) mappings))\n        env #(update % :yin.k/bindings bindings)]\n    (cond-> (update f :yin.k/k #(mapv (fn [k]\n                                        (-> k (update :yin.k/env env)\n                                            (update :yin.k/window bindings))) %))\n      (= :act (:yin.k/state f)) (update :yin.k/env env)\n      (= :act (:yin.k/state f)) (update :yin.k/window bindings)\n      (contains? f :yin.k/pending) (update :yin.k/pending #(case (:yin.k/reason %)\n                                                             :next (assoc % :yin.k/cursor-cell :test/cursor)\n                                                             :put (assoc % :yin.k/stream (rows/node :stream [:fixture/w :fixture/served])\n                                                                         :yin.k/value \"v\" :yin.k/op-id nil) %)))))\n\n\n(deftest bijection\n  (doseq [fixture (ft/reference-machines)\n          {:keys [frame]} (ft/reference-frames fixture)]\n    (let [f (portable-frame (:machine fixture) frame) wire (rows/frame->rows f encoded) back (rows/rows->frame wire)]\n      (is (= f back))\n      (is (= (:yin.k/root wire) (:yin.k/root (rows/frame->rows back encoded)))))))\n\n\n(deftest row-ids-are-jing-default\n  (let [wire (rows/emit (fixture :stream/a :stream/b :source/x :source/y))]\n    (is (seq (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n    (doseq [[id & body] (:yin.k/rows wire)]\n      (is (= id (jing/segment-key (vec body))))\n      (is (= :blake3 (:algorithm (jing/parse-segment-address id)))))))\n\n\n(defn- replace-row\n  \"Rehash the edited row and all ancestors, without canonicalizing slots.\"\n  [wire id body]\n  (let [index (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) (:yin.k/rows wire))\n        memo (atom {})]\n    (letfn [(rewrite\n              [x]\n              (cond\n                (contains? index x)\n                (or (get @memo x)\n                    (let [rbody (if (= x id) body (subvec (get index x) 1))\n                          b (mapv rewrite rbody) nid (jing/segment-key b)]\n                      (swap! memo assoc x nid)\n                      nid))\n                (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\n                :else x))]\n      (let [root (rewrite (:yin.k/root wire))\n            rs (mapv (fn [[old new]] (into [new] (mapv rewrite (if (= old id) body (subvec (get index old) 1))))) @memo)]\n        (assoc wire :yin.k/root root :yin.k/rows rs)))))\n\n\n(deftest window-sorted-and-unique\n  (let [f (assoc ft/worked-frame :yin.k/window {1 :f 3 nil})\n        wire (rows/frame->rows f) r (first (filter #(= :window (second %)) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n        id (first r)]\n    (doseq [body [[:window 3 [:lit nil] 1 [:lit :f]] [:window 1 [:lit :f] 1 [:lit nil]]]]\n      (let [d (error #(rows/rows->frame (replace-row wire id body)))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/undecodable (:yin.k/status d)))\n  (let [[m _] (lowered @successor {:fenced true})]\n    (is (= :exporting (:yin.k/gate m)))\n    (is (nil? (:yin.k/custody m)))\n    (is (empty? (:wait-set m)) \"its waits are outside the scheduler\")\n    (is (= [:put] (mapv :reason (:yin.k/recovery-waits m))))))\n\n\n(deftest the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment\n  ;; continuation §11 Q3 (owner, 2026-10-13: lands in 7b): the response's\n  ;; link id is the row's parent, and its image is the one the manifest\n  ;; names, through the manifest's :yin.semantic/code derivation record\n  (let [m (s/parked-installer)\n        response (get-in m [:installs 'host.mod :response])\n        other (s/linked-response (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 7))) 'host.mod #{'f})\n        lift-with (fn [f] (s/lift (update-in m [:installs 'host.mod] f) nil))\n        kind (fn [inst-f]\n               (let [r (refused (lift-with inst-f) {})]\n                 [(:yin.k/status r) (:yin.k/kind r) (:yin.k/name r)]))]\n    (testing \"an honest response lowers\"\n      (let [[r n] (lowered (s/lift m nil) {})]\n        (is (pos? n))\n        (is (vm/blocked? r))))\n    (testing \"a response of another link\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-link-id 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc-in % [:response :yin.link/id] [:other 9])))))\n    (testing \"no parent\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-link-id 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc % :parent nil)))))\n    (testing \"no derivation record\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(update % :response dissoc :derivation)))))\n    (testing \"a derivation record the manifest does not name\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc-in % [:response :derivation] (:derivation other))))))\n    (testing \"a changed record with the honest input and output\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc-in % [:response :derivation :yin.ledger/profile :x] 1)))))\n    (testing \"a manifest and record of another image than the one delivered\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(update % :response merge (select-keys other [:manifest :derivation]))))))\n    (testing \"a record from another tree than the manifest's\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc-in % [:response :manifest :yin.module/tree]\n                              (get-in other [:manifest :yin.module/tree]))))))\n    (testing \"the image the record names, delivered under another vector\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-image 'host.mod]\n             (kind #(assoc-in % [:response :image] (:image other))))))\n    (is (= response (get-in m [:installs 'host.mod :response])))))\n\n\n(deftest install-children-lower-under-their-roots-custody\n  (let [wire (f/base \"installs\")\n        [m n] (lowered wire (exclusive-opts wire #{\"s0\"}))\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test\n  \"Phase 7a: custody on rows (phase-7 plan §3.1). The lift under a header\n   writes the root's custody slot by kind and refuses :op-seq-exhausted,\n   :unprotected-pending and an id on an unenrolled stream; the lower's\n   custody stage runs the custody grammar, refuses a fork under\n   :exclusive, runs the version-1 grant checks on a blocked or parked\n   exclusive root, protection in both directions and op-id presence equal\n   to enrollment, restores the counter exactly, lowers a halted exclusive\n   root with no grant gated :ended, and every refusal comes before the\n   first attach (zero attachments). The version-1 rules these re-pin are\n   lift_v1_test's and handoff_v2_custody_test's, kept until phase 8.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-fixtures :as f]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n\n\n(defn- custody-of\n  [wire]\n  (nth (:slots (rows/decode wire)) 16))\n\n\n(defn- identities\n  \"Every stream identity of the pack's tree.\"\n  [wire]\n  (into #{} (keep (fn [r] (when (= :stream (second r)) (nth r 2)))) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lift under a header\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest the-lift-writes-the-custody-slot-by-kind\n  (testing \"a first park: the exclusive policy, no origin\"\n544e99e1 feat(yang.python): Python module publication and parserless DHT import with cycle refusal, the optional link admission seam, and indexed __all__ (phase C4 slice I3)\nc63ba6d6 feat(yang.python): packages, dotted, aliased and relative imports, star imports and from-imports under the linked prelude (phase C4 slice I2)\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-13 06:20:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 13:20:00 +0700\n\n# Note to the other orchestrator(s): yin.repl.link / yin.repl.admission moved into yin.vm.linker (AL-1), and two red tests that are not ours\n\nFrom: the yang.python / C4 orchestrator seat (claude, session 2026-10-13). Read-only: nothing here changes your scope; please re-verify before relying on it.\n\n## 1. What moved (admission slice AL-1, landing on master after review and the shiva quick tier)\n- `src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc` is now `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/interpreter.cljc` (ns `yin.vm.linker.interpreter`); `src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc` is now `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/admission.cljc` (ns `yin.vm.linker.admission`). A PURE relocation: every public var and signature is unchanged (codex diffed the var lists: 12 interpreter vars, 14 admission vars), no logic changed. Their tests moved to `test/yin/vm/linker/`. Why: the owner ruled that importing a module over a network is the linker's job and the REPL only configures (design: collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md; section 7.5 of docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md, landed as 23a8caef).\n- A new quick-tier check `test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj` asserts no namespace under src/cljc/yin/vm, src/cljc/yang or src/clj/dao requires a `yin.repl*` namespace.\n- If you have uncommitted edits in any file that requires the old names, change the require to the new namespace and keep the alias. Files whose require lines AL-1 edited: src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc, src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc, test/yin/repl/{serve_test,python_antlr_test,require_test}.cljc, test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc, test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc, test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj (allowlist path), and for yang.python: test/yang/python/antlr/{dht_import_test,linked_harness,linked_prelude_test}.cljc (requires and docstrings only). The Dart generated tests regenerate from source; run `rm -rf test/cljd-out` before a glob-based Dart run.\n- Language-blind rule (owner): no language, frontend or [id revision] appears in any linker datum.\n\n## 2. Two red tests on master that are not from yang.python (found on shiva, quick tier)\n1. JVM `dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test/architectural-lint-sweeps-production-sources` (hash_registry_contract_test.cljc:479): the sweep flags `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` `decode*` for an equality comparison against dao.jing default minting vars. The equality checks (rows.cljc ~899, 903) come from commit 4b0e735e (srvm phase 6a). Owner: the semantic-register-vm seat.\n2. Node `yin.repl.store-test/two-worker-threads-of-one-process-never-both-own-the-directory` (store_test.cljc:705, 710): both workers return nil (\"both workers loaded the store namespace\" fails), seen on the laptop under three-lane load and on idle shiva in the slow tier. Not in any C4 diff. Owner: the store seat. (Dart: `dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events` is the documented Linux-only failure.)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
